.TH "zelta\-propsync" "8" "" "" "System Manager\(cqs Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]zelta propsync\f[R] \- sync local ZFS properties between dataset
trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]zelta propsync\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]source\f[R]
\f[I]target\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]zelta propsync\f[R] replays local ZFS properties from one dataset
tree to another while preserving target\-only local overrides.
It is used by \f[B]zelta failover\f[R] so a promoted target receives the
operational properties needed to take over service.
.PP
Most users should start with \f[B]zelta\-failover(8)\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Sync local properties before unlocking a standby tree:
.IP
.EX
zelta propsync primary.example.com:tank/service standby.example.com:tank/service
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non\-zero on error.
